Incident: SDD

Purpose:
  Defines incident lifecycle, structure, and response policy.
  Incident is distinct from alert: alert = suspicion, incident =
  confirmed business/system impact.

IncidentLifecycle:
  DETECTED:
    ↓
  TRIAGED:
    - Severity assessment
    - Impact assessment
    - Owner assignment
    ↓
  INVESTIGATING:
    - Collect signals
    - Correlate data
    - Identify root cause
    ↓
  MITIGATING:
    - Immediate fix or workaround
    - Stop bleeding
    ↓
  RESOLVED:
    - Root cause fixed
    - Verification
    ↓
  POSTMORTEM:
    - Timeline
    - Root cause
    - Impact
    - Lessons learned
    ↓
  PREVENTION:
    - Task creation
    - Architecture review
    - Skill update

IncidentStructure:
  ID:
    INC-YYYYMMDD-NNN

  Severity:
    S1 (Critical): System down, data loss
    S2 (Major): Core functionality broken
    S3 (Minor): Non-critical feature broken
    S4 (Low): Minimal impact

  Detected:
    - alert: ALT-xxx
    - time: timestamp

  Impact:
    - affected_services
    - affected_users
    - business_impact

  Timeline:
    - start
    - detected
    - mitigated
    - resolved

  RootCause:
    - cause
    - confidence
    - evidence

  Task:
    - TASK-xxx (if created)

  Status:
    - DETECTED
    - TRIAGED
    - INVESTIGATING
    - MITIGATING
    - RESOLVED
    - POSTMORTEM
    - PREVENTION

IncidentResponse:
  S1:
    - Immediate page
    - War room
    - All-hands if needed
    - Rollback considered
  S2:
    - Page on-call
    - Fix within SLA
  S3:
    - Ticket created
    - Fix within 24h
  S4:
    - Next sprint

CrossLayer:
  Alerting: Alerts trigger incident detection
  Diagnostics: Diagnostic flow feeds investigation
  Task: Incident creates fix task
  Architecture: Recurring incidents trigger architecture review
  Skill: Outdated skills trigger skill update proposal

State: +
  